{:adr/id "2607120100"
 :adr/title "kami-engine app rendering standard is cljs-direct WebGPU (org-w3-webgpu) where no existing engine boundary is reused"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-07-12"
 :adr/related ["2607051400-kami-engine-webgpu-sdk-consolidation"
               "2607052000-kami-engine-sdk-svelte-retirement-cljs-migration"
               "2607032100-consolidate-engine-into-kami-engine-clj"
               "2607100030-kotoba-kami-engine-host-imports"
               "2607100100-kami-app-amenominaka"]

 :gap "network-isekai's renderer (kami.webgpu -> w3.webgpu/org-w3-webgpu) was already pure cljs, no Rust, no wasm, but that repo's own ADR-0001 sec1 / ADR-0002 still described a Rust kami-web renderer whose source was removed upstream 2026-07-01 (issue #49) -- documentation debt, not a code gap. Separately, kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk (renamed 2026-07-10 from kami-engine-sdk-clj) has a real Rust wasm-bindgen GPU backend (kami.backend.browser -> kami-clj-host -> kami-render)."

 :correction "initial read treated kami-engine-sdk's Rust backend as the gap CLAUDE.md's no-new-Rust rule targets. Reading that SDK's own ARCHITECTURE.md ('Decision summary: the three forks') surfaced that keeping the Rust backend is a DELIBERATE, REASONED design fork ('Keep the Rust backend... Not Rust applies to everything above the GPU, not the GPU driver itself'; non-goal: 'Not a wgpu re-implementation in clj/cljs'). This is exactly CLAUDE.md's own carve-out (existing exposed Rust/WASM boundary, called as-is) not a violation of it -- writing a parallel org-w3-webgpu backend would mean re-implementing kami-render's battle-tested pipelines, contradicting the SDK's own stated non-goal. No kami.backend.web was implemented; none is planned by this ADR."

 :decision "where no existing, maintained rendering engine is already bound in (network-isekai, kami-app-amenominaka), standard app-level rendering = cljs kami.webgpu/w3.webgpu (org-w3-webgpu) direct, no new Rust, no new wasm-bindgen GPU backend. Where an existing, battle-tested engine boundary IS already reused as-is (kami-engine-sdk's kami.backend.browser -> kami-render), that stays -- it is the legitimate exception CLAUDE.md's own rule describes, not something to demote or replace. kotoba.kami-host's wasm-hosted deterministic ECS (guest logic, ADR-2607100030) is explicitly out of scope and unaffected -- different concern, stays wasm-hosted by design."

 :network-isekai-instance
 {:repo "gftdcojp/network-isekai"
  :local-adr "0033-renderer-rust-free-and-at6-texan-3d.md"
  :change "corrected isekai/render_ir.cljc docstring + README.md renderer description (stale Rust kami-web claim); at6-texan moved off :render/sprite2d onto the pure-3D render-IR path with a real altitude (Climb axis + z-read in entities->instances) mechanic"}

 :kami-engine-sdk-backend
 {:repo "kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk-clj (GitHub-renamed to kami-engine-sdk 2026-07-10, redirect still live under the old remote URL)"
  :outcome "no change -- kami.backend.browser (Rust kami-clj-host wasm-bindgen -> kami-render) remains the one real IGpuBackend implementation and stays default, per :correction above"}

 :verification {:network-isekai "loaded /games/gftd/at6-texan in a real browser via claude-in-chrome/Playwright: no console errors, pure-3D render, Climb axis changes visible altitude + HUD stat, altitude-gated signal release, hangar victory flow unchanged"}

 :follow-up ["kami-engine-web / kami-engine-render umbrella scaffolds still stub-only -- filling them with first-class org-w3-webgpu modules deferred, and only for the case where no existing engine boundary is being reused"
             "kami-engine-sdk-svelte's separate Rust/wgpu-wasm VRM viewer path untouched (already mid-retirement under ADR-2607052000)"
             "manifest/west.yml still registers this SDK repo as kami-engine-sdk-clj (pre-rename name) -- updating the manifest entry to the current kami-engine-sdk name is a separate, low-urgency follow-up not done in this pass"]}
